1
00:00:00,050 --> 00:00:04,752
On Sunday evening, Aziz opens the marketplace app and taps My orders.

2
00:00:04,802 --> 00:00:07,200
He wants to see when the new kettle arrives.

3
00:00:07,250 --> 00:00:11,616
But Aziz is still at level one, and his orders are personal data.

4
00:00:11,666 --> 00:00:14,136
Should the marketplace simply say no?

5
00:00:14,186 --> 00:00:18,648
In Lesson 21, the token carried the session level, one or two.

6
00:00:18,698 --> 00:00:26,520
This lesson shows what an app does when that level is too low: the required level of each app, the step-up, and the trip to the master app.

7
00:00:26,570 --> 00:00:28,488
Start with the apps themselves.

8
00:00:28,538 --> 00:00:34,248
Each app of the bank is written in the installation with a name, a kind and a required level.

9
00:00:34,298 --> 00:00:36,312
The mobile bank is one app.

10
00:00:36,362 --> 00:00:40,968
The marketplace app is another, and the marketplace web profile is a third.

11
00:00:41,018 --> 00:00:42,960
The credit service is one more.

12
00:00:43,010 --> 00:00:45,720
The bank sets the required level of each app.

13
00:00:45,770 --> 00:00:46,080
In fact, the installation will not start until at least one app has a required level.

14
00:00:46,130 --> 00:00:50,544
An app with required level one is usable right after registration.

15
00:00:50,594 --> 00:00:55,416
Aziz registered, set his password, and could browse the marketplace at once.

16
00:00:55,466 --> 00:00:58,752
Now the rule that changes everything for an app team.

17
00:00:58,802 --> 00:01:05,184
Each app must ask for level two before it shows personal data: orders, addresses or cards.

18
00:01:05,234 --> 00:01:07,224
The app does not guess the level.

19
00:01:07,274 --> 00:01:10,800
It reads it from the identity summary, or straight from the token.

20
00:01:10,850 --> 00:01:14,976
So the marketplace sees level one, and My orders needs level two.

21
00:01:15,026 --> 00:01:17,976
Here is the part I think most teams get wrong.

22
00:01:18,026 --> 00:01:22,248
The easy answer is to refuse, with an error and a sad face.

23
00:01:22,298 --> 00:01:24,744
heeyID never refuses a customer here.

24
00:01:24,794 --> 00:01:27,888
Instead, the marketplace calls the step-up.

25
00:01:27,938 --> 00:01:29,736
The answer has three parts.

26
00:01:29,786 --> 00:01:31,488
The current level: one.

27
00:01:31,538 --> 00:01:33,384
The required level: two.

28
00:01:33,434 --> 00:01:39,720
And the checks that give level two: consent, a full proofing with MyID, and a phone check.

29
00:01:39,770 --> 00:01:41,376
So the answer is not no.

30
00:01:41,426 --> 00:01:43,248
It is the way up.

31
00:01:43,298 --> 00:01:45,216
But the marketplace is a side app.

32
00:01:45,266 --> 00:01:48,696
It has no MyID inside, and it never checks a face.

33
00:01:48,746 --> 00:01:52,824
So the step-up answer also says: continue in the mobile bank.

34
00:01:52,874 --> 00:01:58,200
If a side app tries to open a proofing anyway, the platform refuses that request.

35
00:01:58,250 --> 00:02:04,656
MyID runs only in the master app, because only the master app moves money and carries the strongest protection.

36
00:02:04,706 --> 00:02:09,216
The marketplace shows Aziz one button: continue in the mobile bank.

37
00:02:09,266 --> 00:02:11,784
He taps it, and the mobile bank opens.

38
00:02:11,834 --> 00:02:15,936
Now the checks run, one by one, and you have seen each of them already.

39
00:02:15,986 --> 00:02:19,272
First, the consent screen, from Lesson 14.

40
00:02:19,322 --> 00:02:21,528
Aziz reads it and accepts.

41
00:02:21,578 --> 00:02:26,208
Then MyID, from Lesson 15: his face and his passport.

42
00:02:26,258 --> 00:02:28,920
Then he confirms the data that MyID returned.

43
00:02:28,970 --> 00:02:33,792
Then the phone check, from Lesson 18: his number against the numbers that MyID knows.

44
00:02:33,842 --> 00:02:37,224
Everything matches, and his status becomes Confirmed.

45
00:02:37,274 --> 00:02:39,096
Three things change at once.

46
00:02:39,146 --> 00:02:41,496
Aziz is now at level two.

47
00:02:41,546 --> 00:02:43,080
His phone becomes Trusted.

48
00:02:43,130 --> 00:02:47,328
And the gateway issues a new mobile bank token with level two.

49
00:02:47,378 --> 00:02:48,696
Notice what did not happen.

50
00:02:48,746 --> 00:02:50,736
No app gave Aziz level two.

51
00:02:50,786 --> 00:02:53,592
No approval gave it, and no operator gave it.

52
00:02:53,642 --> 00:02:56,304
Only the MyID check gives level two.

53
00:02:56,354 --> 00:02:58,200
That is a hard rule of the platform.

54
00:02:58,250 --> 00:03:02,664
The level belongs to the person, so it is the same in every app.

55
00:03:02,714 --> 00:03:06,528
But a session has its own level, and that is a different thing.

56
00:03:06,578 --> 00:03:10,992
In the mobile bank, a session has level two only on a trusted device.

57
00:03:11,042 --> 00:03:16,608
If Aziz opens the mobile bank on a different phone, that session starts at level one.

58
00:03:16,658 --> 00:03:22,296
In a side app, a session gets level two only after Aziz approves it in the master app.

59
00:03:22,346 --> 00:03:24,960
Lesson 26 shows that approval.

60
00:03:25,010 --> 00:03:32,928
So back in the marketplace, the person is at level two, and the marketplace session reaches level two through that approval.

61
00:03:32,978 --> 00:03:34,440
I think this is a good design.

62
00:03:34,490 --> 00:03:38,760
The person proves who he is once, in one strong place.

63
00:03:38,810 --> 00:03:42,192
Every other app borrows that proof, and never copies it.

64
00:03:42,242 --> 00:03:44,064
To recap.

65
00:03:44,114 --> 00:03:45,984
Each app has a required level.

66
00:03:46,034 --> 00:03:50,088
When the session level is too low, the platform does not refuse.

67
00:03:50,138 --> 00:03:52,368
It answers with the level and the checks.

68
00:03:52,418 --> 00:03:55,008
And the checks run only in the master app.

69
00:03:55,058 --> 00:03:58,800
Tonight, Aziz logs out of the mobile bank on his trusted phone.

70
00:03:58,850 --> 00:04:02,688
Tomorrow morning, on the same phone, his session is gone.

71
00:04:02,738 --> 00:04:04,560
How does he get back in?

72
00:04:04,610 --> 00:04:07,152
Next: login on a known device.
